## Tech Stack:

- Backend: Node.js with Nest.js
- Database: Supabase
- Authentication: Supabase Auth
- API Documentation: Swagger/OpenAPI
- Testing: Jest with Supertest
- CI/CD: GitHub Actions

## Workflow Setup

- Use pnpm when adding dependencies
- Be mindful if dependencies are for development and use the appropriate flags
- Follow conventional commits (feat:, fix:, docs:, etc.)
- Create feature branches from develop branch
- Use meaningful branch names (feature/, bugfix/, hotfix/)
- Review and update dependencies regularly for security

## Coding Standards

- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Use proper TypeScript types for all variables, functions and return types
- Use barrel imports
- Implement proper error handling and input validation
- Always use relative imports
- Follow consistent naming conventions:
  - PascalCase for classes, interfaces, and types
  - camelCase for variables, functions, and methods
  - UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for constants
- Maximum line length: 100 characters
- Use async/await over raw promises
- Implement proper logging using a logging framework

## Best Practices

- Ensure secure, efficient code following RESTful API best practices
- Respect SOLID principles
- Focus on performance and readability
- Implement proper request validation using DTOs
- Use dependency injection for better testability
- Implement rate limiting for API endpoints
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Implement proper error handling middleware
- Use database transactions where necessary
- Implement proper caching strategies
- Follow the principle of least privilege
- Write comprehensive unit and integration tests
- Maintain test coverage above 80%

## Security Guidelines

- Implement proper authentication and authorization
- Use HTTPS for all endpoints
- Implement CORS properly
- Sanitize all user inputs
- Use parameterized queries for database operations
- Implement proper session management
- Use secure password hashing (bcrypt)
- Implement request size limits
- Use security headers (helmet)
- Regular security audits and updates

## Documentation Standards

- Use JSDoc for code documentation
- Maintain up-to-date API documentation
- Document all environment variables
- Include setup instructions in README
- Document database schema changes
- Add comments for complex business logic
- Create architecture decision records (ADRs)

## Performance Guidelines

- Implement proper database indexing
- Use pagination for list endpoints
- Optimize database queries
- Implement caching where appropriate
- Use compression for responses
- Optimize asset delivery
- Monitor and optimize memory usage
- Implement proper connection pooling

